{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he shall inquire for him by the judgment of the Urim.</b> He did not mention the Tummim, and this indicates that the Urim were the principal of the names through whose power the letters would light up before the eyes of the priest to know by them future events, and the Tummim were only to pair the letters one with another, to complete them in the joining of the words, until the heart of the priest would be complete (תמים) in their knowledge and combination. Therefore he mentioned what is principal and was silent concerning the Tummim; but the Urim were never without the Tummim, for the two are one thing and the two together are the perfection of the matter, and they were placed between the folds of the breastplate. And from this verse the Sages, blessed be memory, in Yoma, chapter 'Ba Lo,' derived: a decree of a prophet may be retracted, but a decree of the Urim and Tummim is not retracted, as it is said, ״ושאל לו במשפט האורים״ — just as a judgment (משפט) is not retracted, so too a decree of the Urim and Tummim. And now He said to Moses: Joshua in your place — ״והוא וכל בני ישראל על פיו יצאו״, that is, by the word of Eleazar they go out, and ״ועל פיו יבאו״, that is, the sovereignty shall not depart from your tribe." "<b>He and all the children of Israel with him, and all the congregation.</b> The congregation is included within 'all the children of Israel,' but it says 'and all the congregation' — even the dissenters, who are called 'congregation' everywhere, all of them shall be subordinate to him. And the Sages, blessed be memory, interpreted: 'and all the congregation' — these are the Sanhedrin, who are the eyes of the congregation, the distinguished ones within the congregation, and therefore he specified 'the congregation.' And that which he mentioned in the command, ״והעמדת אתו לפני אלעזר הכהן ולפני כל העדה״, is a proof and reinforcement for the words of the Sages, blessed be memory. And so too he mentioned in the account of the deed: ״ויעמידהו לפני אלעזר הכהן ולפני כל העדה״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:40.616368334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}